<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="64617" href="schedule/2015/fall/CS/598/64617.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2015" href="schedule/2015.xml">2015</calendarYear><term id="120158" href="schedule/2015/fall.xml">Fall 2015</term><subject id="CS" href="schedule/2015/fall/CS.xml">Computer Science</subject><course id="598" href="schedule/2015/fall/CS/598.xml">Special Topics</course></parents><sectionNumber>DHP</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Scripting Lang - Design Implem</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Prerequisites: Graduate standing  Scripting languages are widely used for all types of applications. They are the programming languages of the web and are also widely used for scientific computing and data analytics. This course will discuss the main characteristics of scripting languages, their capabilities for parallelism, their impact on productivity and performance, and interpreter and compiler techniques to implement them. Reading assignments will include research papers and class notes.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2015-08-24Z</startDate><endDate>2015-12-09Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="S3 ">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>09:00 AM</start><end>10:15 AM</end><daysOfTheWeek>MW     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>1105</roomNumber><buildingName>Siebel Center for Comp Sci</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Padua" firstName="D">Padua, D</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>